1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,080
Nearly every business site stores phone numbers and addresses.

2
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:09,100
This video shows the CrestApps Phone Field and Address Field:

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:13,180
why they exist, how to add them to a content type, how editors

4
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:17,920
fill them in, and how the list of countries and address suggestions work.

5
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:25,115
A branch has a front desk number.

6
00:00:25,115 --> 00:00:27,443
A venue has a street address.

7
00:00:27,443 --> 00:00:30,038
A customer has a billing address.

8
00:00:30,038 --> 00:00:32,500
Contact details are everywhere.

9
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:37,594
In a plain text box, a phone number can be typed with spaces,

10
00:00:37,594 --> 00:00:43,040
dashes or no country code, so the site cannot dial it, text it, or compare it.

11
00:00:43,790 --> 00:00:45,470
Addresses are harder.

12
00:00:45,470 --> 00:00:49,764
The United States has a state and a ZIP code, Canada a province

13
00:00:49,764 --> 00:00:54,431
and a postal code, and the United Kingdom a post town and a postcode.

14
00:00:54,431 --> 00:00:56,920
One fixed form suits none of them.

15
00:00:57,670 --> 00:01:01,301
The Phone Field and the Address Field take the guesswork out.

16
00:01:01,301 --> 00:01:06,070
They follow the country, check what is typed, and keep it in one consistent shape.

17
00:01:10,270 --> 00:01:14,334
The Phone Field has a country flag picker, formats the number as you

18
00:01:14,334 --> 00:01:17,300
type, and stores it in the international format.

19
00:01:18,050 --> 00:01:22,684
The Address Field lays itself out the way the chosen country writes addresses,

20
00:01:22,684 --> 00:01:26,160
and checks the postal code against the state or province.

21
00:01:26,910 --> 00:01:31,761
The Address Countries feature keeps the countries your site serves as a list

22
00:01:31,761 --> 00:01:34,660
that you can rename, add to or remove from.

23
00:01:35,410 --> 00:01:37,940
Address suggestions are optional.

24
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:43,260
With a Google Places key, the field suggests addresses as a street is typed.

25
00:01:47,472 --> 00:01:53,656
Open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, and edit the type that needs a phone number.

26
00:01:53,656 --> 00:01:55,612
Here it is Branch Office.

27
00:01:56,984 --> 00:02:01,405
Click Add Field, type the name editors will see, such as Main phone,

28
00:02:01,405 --> 00:02:03,974
and choose Phone Field from the list.

29
00:02:03,974 --> 00:02:06,124
Then click Save and Configure.

30
00:02:07,337 --> 00:02:11,300
Required makes editors enter a number before they can save.

31
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:14,227
The Hint is help text under the phone box.

32
00:02:14,679 --> 00:02:19,135
Initial country decides which flag is selected when the box is empty.

33
00:02:19,135 --> 00:02:24,721
Globe selects no country, Current culture uses the editor's country, and Specific always

34
00:02:24,721 --> 00:02:27,039
starts on the country you choose.

35
00:02:27,496 --> 00:02:31,895
If most of your numbers are in one country, choose Specific and pick

36
00:02:31,895 --> 00:02:33,857
it, here the United States.

37
00:02:33,857 --> 00:02:35,106
Save the field.

38
00:02:39,285 --> 00:02:41,792
Add an address in the same way.

39
00:02:41,792 --> 00:02:48,025
Click Add Field, name it Location, choose Address Field, and click Save and Configure.

40
00:02:48,476 --> 00:02:53,504
Required forces an address to be entered, and the Hint appears above it.

41
00:02:53,504 --> 00:02:57,565
Ask for a recipient name, Ask for a company and Ask for a

42
00:02:57,565 --> 00:03:00,272
phone number choose the extra lines.

43
00:03:00,272 --> 00:03:04,656
A branch needs only the company, so untick the recipient name.

44
00:03:05,121 --> 00:03:11,423
Countries offered limits the choice to the countries you serve, here the United States and Canada.

45
00:03:11,423 --> 00:03:14,090
Leave it empty to offer every country.

46
00:03:14,090 --> 00:03:17,241
Default country is where a new address starts.

47
00:03:17,702 --> 00:03:19,018
Save the field.

48
00:03:19,018 --> 00:03:22,842
The content type now has a phone number and an address.

49
00:03:27,053 --> 00:03:28,979
Create a new Branch Office.

50
00:03:28,979 --> 00:03:33,529
The editor sees the Main phone box with the United States flag selected,

51
00:03:33,529 --> 00:03:35,863
and the Location address below it.

52
00:03:36,313 --> 00:03:40,790
Click the flag to choose another country, here Canada, and type the number.

53
00:03:40,790 --> 00:03:44,383
The box formats it as you type, and the item keeps the full

54
00:03:44,383 --> 00:03:47,423
international number with the country you picked.

55
00:03:47,875 --> 00:03:53,107
In the address, the country comes first and the rest of the form follows it.

56
00:03:53,107 --> 00:03:57,575
For the United States, the form asks for a State and a ZIP code.

57
00:03:58,027 --> 00:04:02,435
Choose Canada, and the form changes to Province and Postal code, in the

58
00:04:02,435 --> 00:04:04,896
order Canadian addresses are written.

59
00:04:04,896 --> 00:04:09,647
Fill in the street and the city, choose a province, and type the postal code.

60
00:04:10,097 --> 00:04:12,903
The address is checked against its country.

61
00:04:12,903 --> 00:04:17,198
A postal code that does not belong to the chosen province is refused,

62
00:04:17,198 --> 00:04:19,317
and the field says what to fix.

63
00:04:19,771 --> 00:04:22,194
Choose the right province, and publish.

64
00:04:22,194 --> 00:04:26,502
The saved item shows the phone number grouped for reading, and the address

65
00:04:26,502 --> 00:04:28,871
printed the way its country writes it.

66
00:04:33,090 --> 00:04:38,708
With Address Countries on, every country is a content item of the type Country.

67
00:04:38,708 --> 00:04:43,070
Open Content, Content Items, and filter by the Country type.

68
00:04:43,525 --> 00:04:47,663
Edit a country to rename it, or use New Country to add one.

69
00:04:47,663 --> 00:04:53,265
Delete the countries your site does not serve, and the fields offer only the rest.

70
00:04:57,484 --> 00:04:59,899
Open Settings, Address suggestions.

71
00:04:59,899 --> 00:05:04,908
The page explains that suggestions come from Google Places, and that you create

72
00:05:04,908 --> 00:05:08,384
a key for the Places API in the Google Cloud console.

73
00:05:08,873 --> 00:05:12,635
Paste the key in the Google Places API key box and save.

74
00:05:12,635 --> 00:05:16,154
The key is kept on the server and never shown again.

75
00:05:16,154 --> 00:05:19,673
Without a key, people type their address themselves.

76
00:05:23,873 --> 00:05:29,893
Branch, office and venue pages with a clickable phone number and a correct address.

77
00:05:30,643 --> 00:05:35,443
Contacts and customers whose phone numbers must be dialled or texted.

78
00:05:36,193 --> 00:05:40,153
Billing and shipping addresses that follow each country's rules.

79
00:05:40,903 --> 00:05:46,303
Sites that serve only some countries, with exactly those countries on offer.

80
00:05:48,303 --> 00:05:52,258
Add the Phone Field and the Address Field to a content type once,

81
00:05:52,258 --> 00:05:56,936
and every editor gets a box that follows the country and checks what is typed.

82
00:05:56,936 --> 00:05:58,383
Thanks for watching.

